---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="ReflectMe — Case Study | Mayank Solan">
  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <!-- Back Navigation -->
    <header
      class="fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-40 border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--background)]/95 backdrop-blur-md"
    >
      <nav class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 lg:px-8">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
          ← Back
        </a>
        <span class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">ReflectMe</span>
        <div></div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- Case Study Content -->
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-32 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <div class="mb-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--terracotta)]">
            02 / Product
          </span>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">ReflectMe</h1>
          <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
            A feedback and reflection platform that helps people collect meaningful feedback from
            peers, analyze patterns with AI, and turn insights into actionable growth.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {
            ["React", "Vite", "Supabase", "PostgreSQL", "Groq (AI)", "Resend", "Tailwind CSS"].map(
              (tech) => (
                <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--sage-soft)] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--foreground)]">
                  {tech}
                </span>
              )
            )
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Problem -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The Problem</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
          <p>
            Feedback is uncomfortable. It's scattered across Slack threads, email, annual reviews,
            and conversations. Most people never systematically collect it, and when they do, the
            data sits unanalyzed. Useful patterns go unnoticed.
          </p>
          <p>
            How could we make feedback collection frictionless, insightful, and actionable? What if
            AI could find the story hiding in dozens of one-off comments?
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Solution -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The Solution</h2>

        <div class="space-y-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Send Feedback Requests</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Users create feedback requests and invite peers via email. Invitees land on a simple
              form with 3 question categories: Strengths (what you excel at), Growth Areas (where to
              improve), and Observations (patterns you notice). Responses are anonymous by default,
              removing social friction.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Real-Time Overview Dashboard</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              As responses trickle in, the owner sees live aggregates: response count, sentiment
              distribution (Strengths / Growth / Observations shown as percentage breakdowns), and
              response status. The dashboard is immediately actionable — no waiting for all
              responses to review patterns.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">AI-Powered Insights</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Using Groq's LLM (free tier, fast inference), ReflectMe analyzes all feedback and
              generates a natural language summary: "Your feedback consistently highlights strong
              ownership and problem-solving. Growth areas center on delegation and communication
              under tight deadlines." This AI insight surfaces themes that individual comments might
              not reveal.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Full Feedback History</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              All feedback responses are archived. Users can tag feedback with topics, revisit old
              reflections to see growth over time, and share curated feedback with mentors or
              managers for coaching conversations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Email Notifications</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              The owner receives an email summary each time a new response arrives. Supabase Edge
              Functions integrate with Resend to send templated, branded emails with a preview of
              the feedback and a link to the live dashboard.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Technical Architecture -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Technical Architecture</h2>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Frontend: React + Vite</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Fast dev experience with Vite. React Router handles navigation. Dark/light theme
              toggle persisted to localStorage. All theming uses CSS custom properties (<code
                class="font-mono text-sm">--bg</code
              >,
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">--surface</code>, <code class="font-mono text-sm"
                >--text</code
              >, <code class="font-mono text-sm">--brand</code>) for seamless theme switching
              without component changes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">State Management: React Context</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Two contexts handle all shared state: <code class="font-mono text-sm"
                >AuthContext</code
              > (Supabase auth, user profile, session), and <code class="font-mono text-sm"
                >ThemeContext</code
              > (dark/light toggle). Both are provided at the app root, ensuring consistent auth state
              and theme across routes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Backend: Supabase + PostgreSQL</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Five tables with RLS enabled: <code class="font-mono text-sm">profiles</code>,
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">feedback_requests</code>, <code
                class="font-mono text-sm">feedback_responses</code
              >,
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">reactions</code> (emoji reactions on feedback). Auth is
              handled via Supabase Auth (Google OAuth, email/password, password reset). Profile rows are
              auto-created via DB trigger on signup.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">AI Insights: Groq LLM</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Free tier with fast inference. On request completion, the dashboard calls the AI
              endpoint with all feedback text. Groq analyzes patterns and returns a natural-language
              summary. Results are cached to avoid repeated calls.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Email Notifications: Resend</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Supabase Edge Functions (PostgreSQL triggers → HTTP calls) invoke Resend API to send
              templated emails when new feedback arrives. Emails include a preview snippet and a
              link to view on the dashboard.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Analytics: PostHog (Optional)</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              PostHog SDK tracks user behavior (page views, feedback submissions, AI insight views)
              for product insights. Optional (disabled if no API key in env).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Feedback Visibility Model -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Feedback Visibility & Privacy</h2>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)]">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--sage-soft)]">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Type</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Default Visibility</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Owner Can</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border)]">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Positive Feedback</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Public</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Hide / Show</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Constructive Feedback</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Private</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Publish / Keep Private</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Insights</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Private</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Publish / Keep Private</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
          This model respects the awkwardness of growth feedback — constructive comments are private
          by default, giving owners space to reflect before deciding to share with others. Positive
          feedback surfaces publicly to build confidence and attract opportunities.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Auth Flow -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Auth & Security</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Signup & Profile Creation</h3>
            <p>
              Username + display name are stored as Supabase auth metadata. A DB trigger
              automatically creates the profile row, avoiding the need for an extra signup form.
              Google OAuth is supported for social login.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Password Reset</h3>
            <p>
              "Forgot password?" triggers Supabase's built-in reset flow. Email confirms the reset
              link, redirecting to the ResetPasswordPage where users set a new password.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Row-Level Security (RLS)</h3>
            <p>
              All tables enforce RLS. Users see only their own profile and feedback; they can view
              others' public profiles. Authors see their own submissions even if private. No data
              leaks across users.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 font-semibold">Account Deletion</h3>
            <p>
              The Settings page includes a "Delete Account" button. This calls a Postgres function
              with
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">SECURITY DEFINER</code> that cascades deletion through
              <code class="font-mono text-sm">auth.users</code> (removing the auth record and all dependent
              data).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Lessons & Takeaways -->
      <section class="border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Lessons & Takeaways</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
          <p>
            <strong>Anonymous feedback removes social friction.</strong> People give more honest, detailed
            feedback when identity is hidden. Default anonymity, with optional attribution, balances honesty
            and accountability.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Realtime aggregates beat waiting for all responses.</strong> Live dashboards showing
            response count, sentiment, and preliminary themes reduce the anxiety of feedback collection
            and surface patterns early.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>AI summarization finds non-obvious patterns.</strong> Human reviewers catch obvious
            themes; LLMs find subtle correlations and meta-patterns that make feedback transformation
            possible, not just collection.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Privacy-first defaults build trust.</strong> By defaulting constructive feedback to
            private, ReflectMe respects the vulnerability of receiving criticism. Owners choose when/if
            to share.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Context matters.</strong> Pairing feedback with source (author, anonymous, timestamp)
            and allowing owners to add private notes creates a rich, actionable record that supports coaching
            and growth conversations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section class="mt-20 flex gap-4 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="rounded-full bg-[var(--foreground)] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-transform hover:-translate-y-0.5"
        >
          ← Back to portfolio
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
